Lets examine just how likely this is, under the assumption that you have
magic resistance, but do not have half spell damage or magic bane.

rndcurse picks will pick between 1 and 3 [inclusive] items to curse. 
This means your chances of any rnd curse choosing your blessed bag of holding
twice in an inventory of n items is:

1/3*[1/n^2] + 1/3*[(3n-2)/n^3] = (4n-2)/(3*n^3)

So maybe you have ~35-40 items, and this gives will happen with probability 
~1/1000.

Now, that of course, assumes 1 rndcurse in the given turn- if 2 rndcurses 
happen in one turn, the probability goes to

[1/(3*n) + 2*(n-1)/(3*n^2)+ (n-1)^2/n^3]^2 
+ 2*(4n-2)/(3*n^3) 
- [(4n-2)/(3*n^3)]^2.

Ignoring the probability that two rndcurses happen in one turn [which
requires either 2 spell casters casting a spell AND it being rndcurse
or 1 spell caster and the intervene() effects (random stuff after you
kill the wizard)].

So for 35 items, you get a probability of about 1/200.

In the event that wizard intervention happens on the astral plane while you
are fighting a spell caster capable of rndcurse, then this may happen about 
1/24 times.

So you can't guarantee that you boh wont go blessed->cursed, but if you have
a reasonably large inventory, you can be 99.9% confident it won't.

